    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376-a3">

                <pb facs="0495" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg415"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The governor of Martinique
                        to Captain Gallagher</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Fort de France</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Captain</hi>: You have been so good as to turn over
                    to us the stores which the United States Government so generously offered to the
                    sufferers of the colony of Martinique.</p>
                <p>Permit me on this occasion to beg you to present to your Government, through the
                    Secretary of War, my personal thanks and the expression of the sincere gratitude
                    of the entire population of the colony which suffered so greatly by the disaster
                    of May 8 last.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L’Heurre.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
